SuiteLoop draws a router table as a plan of one shared loop serving a row of suites: every situation is a room fed by its own drop and valve off the loop, with the start page as the room's way out.

- On the site: a `table` block with `"as": "router"` and `"look": "suite-loop"` (renderer `assets/src/blocks/look-suite-loop.js`); used on ind-cdmo (many clients, one water system). Origin: no concept of its own (quota); adapted from industries.0 / home.4 (situations piped off one manifold) and the page drawing ind-cdmo (suites on a shared loop).
- Markup: limestone band → `div.aq-suite-loop` → `span.__loop` (twin walls, `span.__water`, `span.__arrow`, `span.__beam` collapsed at rest), `ol.__suites` of `li.__suite` → `span.__drop` (`span.__dw` water, `span.__valve` svg), `span.__door` (door swing in the lower wall), `span.__tag` "01", `h3.__t`, `dl.__dl` of `div.__f` (middle columns), `a.__go` (last column).
- Fields: `cols` (situation, water, systems, start with), `rows` (string or {t, link, intent} cells).
- Tokens: walls and pipes `on-limestone` mixes, water `flow`, valves `limestone`; the way out turns `navy` on hover/focus; hovering or focusing a suite sends a `flow` slug along the supply run to its drop, then runs water down the drop.
- Mid widths: three suites a row (only the first row keeps drops). Phones (pass 12, S11/S13; under 860 px): the loop is the header, a twin-wall pipe across the top with its supply chevron; the suites hang off it as a horizontal snap row (one room `min(300px, 86%)`, the next peeking), each on its own drop and valve; no left gutter. The room in view lights its drop (water down) and fills its valve; a dot rail under the row (44 px buttons, `aria-label` = number and situation) jumps between rooms. Rooms in the row share one height; the way out is a 48 px row with a smaller door swing. ind-cdmo.0: 2,879 -> 731 px at 375. The snap behaviour is `AQsnap` (defined in the look JS when missing; shared with the other pass 12 rails): a `[data-snap]` scroller, `[data-snap-to]` buttons in the same `[data-snap-box]`, `.is-snap` on the item in view and `aria-current` on its button; a button scrolls to its item (a jump with reduced motion). Pass 12 verify: the section carries `data-theme="light"` (the limestone band stays light in dark, so the flow marks keep 4.6:1); on wide screens each suite is one `minmax(0, 1fr)` column (no content runs through the walls) and with 6 or more suites (`.is-dense`) the way out aligns with the rows above it and a 24 px door swings under it; the way-out arrow is held to its last word (no-break space). Snap rail (AQsnap): at the rail's end, where the last items cannot reach the start edge, the tapped item keeps the mark until the reader swipes.

## Motion

The loop's walls run round the sheet and the water follows; one by one each suite wipes up, its drop is cut from the loop, the valve seats, the water runs down into the suite and settles back, and the words read in. Once on scroll-in, under 5 s; nothing under reduced motion. Pass 9b: concept ind-cdmo.0 was weak (a drawing-sheet frame round the table), so the look was kept and polished: no overshoot eases; pointing at or focusing a suite sends a slug of water along the loop from the supply chevron to that suite's drop (0.25–0.6 s, power3.out, then fades), ported from Subframe Motion "Animated beam connections" (animated-beam); visitor-driven, may repeat. Pass 12: phones run the same timeline as desktop (the loop is across the top there too), so the vertical-riser branches are gone from motion.js.
- Door (pass 12 C): on desktop a 24 px swing in the right corner of the lower wall, inside the way-out cell's 24 px foot, off the link's line; none at 860 px and under (the snap-row layouts, tablets included: at 601-860 the old door crossed the link). Dark (C verify): the rooms take the band's `--surface-raised` (RC1 stone), with a 14 % flow tint on hover, so the ink stays AA. AQsnap now comes from the shared `assets/src/parts/Snap.js` (the look's own copy is gone).
